.TH "restorePrepare" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
restorePrepare \- enable Restore mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.restorePrepare()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to enable Restore mode in preparation for an online
restore.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[]
.PP
Restore mode blocks both transactional data access and any changes to the
cluster.
User can still commit or rollback a transaction though.
.RE
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens，use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Enable Restore mode for the cluster.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restorePrepare()
\f[]
.fi
